{
  "id": "06-clusters",
  "title": "Folded endings",
  "goal": "Most clusters are just the keys one after another. A few fold into a shorter chord, and a vowel often shares keys with its R.",
  "blocks": [
    { "t": "h", "x": "Clusters in order" },
    { "t": "p", "x": "When the sounds come in steno order, press them all: [[tent|TEPBT]], [[hunt|HUPBT]], [[bend|PWEPBD]], [[sand|SAPBD]], [[hold|HOLD]], [[cold|KOELD]], [[mind|PHOEUPBD]]." },
    { "t": "h", "x": "Clusters that fold" },
    { "t": "p", "x": "Where two sounds would not fit the keys in order, the theory folds them. These are the ones to know:" },
    { "t": "table", "head": ["Sounds", "Keys", "Example"], "rows": [
      ["s + t", "[[-FT]]", "[[best|PWEFT]]"],
      ["s + l, l + f", "[[-FL]]", "[[castle|KAFL]]"],
      ["s + n, s + m", "[[-FPB]] / [[-FPL]]", "[[lesson|HR-FPB]]"],
      ["n + k (bank)", "[[*PBG]]", "[[bank|PWA*PBG]]"],
      ["l + k", "[[-LG]]", "[[silk|S*EULG]]"],
      ["l + b", "[[-BL]]", "[[bulb|*UBL]]"],
      ["l + p (the l is dropped)", "[[-P]]", "[[help|HEP]]"],
      ["l + m (the l is in the m)", "[[-PL]]", "[[film|TPEUPL]]"],
      ["-tion, -sion, -cian", "[[-GS]]", "[[nation|TPH-GS]]"]
    ] },
    { "t": "p", "x": "`-GS` is the *shun* of *nation*, *pension*, *mention*. It is so common it is also a suffix on its own in lesson 10." },
    { "t": "h", "x": "A vowel and its R" },
    { "t": "p", "x": "An *r* after a vowel is not struck separately. The vowel and the `R` form one chord:" },
    { "t": "table", "head": ["Sound", "Keys", "Example"], "rows": [
      ["ar as in {{car}}", "[[AR]]", "[[car|KAR]], [[far|TPAR]]"],
      ["or as in {{more}}", "[[OR]]", "[[more|PHOR]]"],
      ["air as in {{hair}}", "[[AEUR]]", "[[hair|HAEUR]], [[care|KAEUR]]"],
      ["ear as in {{beer}}", "[[AOER]]", "[[beer|PWAOER]]"],
      ["ire as in {{fire}}", "[[AOEUR]]", "[[fire|TPAOEUR]]"],
      ["ur as in {{hurt}}", "[[UR]]", "[[hurt|HURT]]"],
      ["ir as in {{girl}}", "[[EUR]]", "[[girl|TKPWEURL]], [[bird|PWEURD]]"]
    ] },
    { "t": "note", "kind": "warn", "x": "The same shapes also keep spellings apart: [[dear|TKAER]] and [[deer|TKAOER]], [[stair|STAEUR]] and [[stare|STAER]]. Lesson 9 covers that." }
  ],
  "drill": {
    "title": "Clusters and R",
    "pass": 90,
